There are lots of problems with this small function. One thing that might jump out at you is the
presence of 0b11000000. This binary notation is cool; can C do that? Unfortunately, no. A few other
problems relate to this code directly using the custom C extensions:
IE: Interrupt enable bits.
SBUF0: Serial output buffer.
TI_0: Serial transmit buffer empty interrupt. Reading a 1 indicates the buffer is empty.
The uppercase variables actually access micro-controller built-in peripherals. If you want to control
interrupts and output characters, you must use these peripherals. Yes, this is convenient—but it’s not
C.
